  "title": "Checkerboard m-sequence-based c-VEP dataset from",
  "description": "A checkerboard m-sequence-based code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) derivative dataset comprising EEG recordings from 16 healthy subjects across 8 sessions with 3 runs per session. This processed dataset is derived from the original source dataset (DOI: 10.71569/7c67-v596) and evaluates the influence of spatial frequency in visual stimuli for brain-computer interface applications, with 16-channel EEG data sampled at 256 Hz during visual stimulation with two intensity conditions (0.0 and 1.0).",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired from 16 healthy subjects using a standard 1005 montage with 16 channels sampled at 256 Hz (50 Hz line frequency). Each subject completed 8 sessions with 3 runs per session. The experimental paradigm employed checkerboard m-sequence-based visual stimuli presented in two intensity conditions (0.0 and 1.0), with trial intervals of 0-1 second.",
